{"id":"65ddea78-d52b-4ef2-a1b7-ff9c4cb18e32", "recipient":"fe679799-378f-4b64-973a-d55f622dfbba", "sender":"ecae43cd-8523-41fe-87da-7740d6da7e80", "priority":"MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH", "timestamp":"2026-09-22T20:22:47.400984800Z", "renderDetails":{"messageTitle":"Message from Beta Tester (browser)"}, "content":"The chrome_devtools MCP server is not available at all, so physical browser testing could not be initiated.\n\nTroubleshooting Steps:\n1. Check DevToolsActivePort file of user's default Chrome profile (verified at `C:\\Users\\samsung\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\DevToolsActivePort`, pointing to port 9222).\n2. Check that the port is open and accessible.\n3. Verify if there are multiple processes listening on port 9222; if so, kill these processes and ensure only a single instance of Chrome with remote debugging is active.\n\nPlease ensure the chrome_devtools MCP server is running and connected before invoking the browser agent again.", "sourceMetadata":{"tool":{"conversationId":"ecae43cd-8523-41fe-87da-7740d6da7e80", "stepIndex":12, "toolCall":{"id":"call_101158", "name":"send_message", "argumentsJson":"{\"Message\":\"The chrome_devtools MCP server is not available at all, so physical browser testing could not be initiated.\\n\\nTroubleshooting Steps:\\n1. Check DevToolsActivePort file of user's default Chrome profile (verified at `C:\\\\Users\\\\samsung\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\DevToolsActivePort`, pointing to port 9222).\\n2. Check that the port is open and accessible.\\n3. Verify if there are multiple processes listening on port 9222; if so, kill these processes and ensure only a single instance of Chrome with remote debugging is active.\\n\\nPlease ensure the chrome_devtools MCP server is running and connected before invoking the browser agent again.\",\"Recipient\":\"fe679799-378f-4b64-973a-d55f622dfbba\",\"toolAction\":\"Sending status update\",\"toolSummary\":\"Report chrome_devtools MCP failure\"}", "thinkin